The query and report builder
29c-sd-tcl-the-development-tools
The page builds a LIST or SORT sentence on one file of your account and shows it, all the time, in the box at the foot. Choose a file in the File box (Enter); mark its columns in the Columns box (Space marks, and the order marked is the order printed; B breaks on the column and T totals it); set up to six conditions (Enter on a row asks for the item, the operator and the value; J switches and / or); set up to four sort levels; and choose the options: the kind of report (list, count or sum), a heading and a footing, leaving out the record id or the detail lines, and only the first n records. F6 and Shift-F6 move between the boxes (and to the AI line, when the AI is on).
A value is plain text, typed as the query processor reads it for the item (see the query documentation). like and unlike take a pattern: 0X any text, 1A a letter, 3N three digits; put 0X on both sides to find text inside a value. A value holds no quote, backslash, backquote or semicolon, and a heading no more.
R runs the sentence and shows what it printed in a box of its own: nothing else on the screen is written by the query, 2000 lines are kept and the box says how many there were, Up and Down and PgUp and PgDn scroll and Left and Right move sideways. A query on a big file is run in full and cannot be stopped from here: use the first-n option for a trial. A select list that is waiting narrows the query; the box says so. E edits the sentence as text; every sentence is checked again before it runs, and only list, sort, count or sum on the chosen file, with the words and the dictionary items the page knows, will run. A word that sends the output elsewhere or writes (to, saving, lptr, csv, as ...) is refused.
S saves the query as a record of the file &queries& of your account (made after a box when you save the first one). L lists the saved queries in a pick window with their file, kind and sentence; typing narrows the list, Enter loads the one under the cursor, Del deletes it after its name is typed, and Esc closes the list. A loaded query is checked again part by part against the file's dictionary, and what does not fit is dropped and counted. The page needs no gate: it only reads, and writes only that one file.
